        "scope": "in_scope",
        "statement": "Every finite direct sum $\\bigoplus_a\\so_{m_a}(k)$ with $m_a\\ge3$ is the\nderivation algebra of an evolution algebra. Thus Theorem~\\ref{thm:classification}\nanswers exactly the semisimple clause of Question~36 in \\cite[\\S2.2.5, p.~25]{survey}.\nMore generally, over any field of characteristic different from two, every\nnondegenerate symmetric space $(V,b)$ has an evolution algebra $E(b)$ with\n$\\mathbf{Aut}(E(b))\\cong O(b)$ and $\\Der(E(b))\\cong\\so(V,b)$.",
